.TH KILLBILL-TUI 1 "2026-09-09" "killbill-rs 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
killbill-tui \- terminal UI for the killbill-rs daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B killbill-tui
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B killbill-tui
is a full-screen
.BR ratatui (7)-style
client for
.BR killbilld (8).
It shows the live device list, armed state, whitelist, settings, dry-run
results, an event log, a read-only config inspector, and the fenced LUKS-destroy
screen.
.PP
It holds
.B no authority.
The daemon owns the config and the armed state; the TUI only sends the same
control-protocol commands
.BR killbillctl (1)
does. Quitting the TUI, or killing it with
.BR SIGKILL ,
.B never
changes whether the daemon is armed.
.PP
State-changing actions require the process to run as
.B uid 0
(the control socket is mode
.B 0660
owned
.BR root:root ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to the daemon's control socket. Default:
.IR /run/killbilld.sock .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH KEYS
Navigation is menu-driven: arrows and
.B Enter
do everything, letters are accelerators.
.SS Everywhere
.TP
.BR \[u2191] " / " \[u2193] " (" k " / " j )
Move the selection, or scroll.
.TP
.B Enter
Activate the selected item, or confirm a modal.
.TP
.B Esc
Close a modal, otherwise return to the Devices screen.
.TP
.B m
Open the main menu (also closes any other modal).
.TP
.B ?
Help screen.
.TP
.B r
Refresh the current screen \(en or retry the connection while the daemon is
down.
.TP
.B q
Quit immediately. Never disarms the daemon.
.TP
.B Ctrl-C
Quit, from anywhere, including inside a text field.
.SS Devices (home)
.TP
.B Enter
Act on the selected device: add it to, or remove it from, the whitelist.
.SS Whitelist
.TP
.B "Enter (top row)"
Add an entry by typing a
.I vendor:product
id.
.TP
.B "Enter (an entry)"
Edit its max count, or remove it.
.SS Settings
.TP
.B Enter
Toggle or cycle the selected field, applied via the daemon.
.SS Dry-run
.TP
.B r
Run the policy engine again over the current devices.
.SS Event log
.TP
.BR \[u2191] " / " \[u2193]
Scroll back through the stream (pauses following).
.TP
.B p
Freeze or resume following the newest line.
.SS LUKS destroy
.TP
.B Enter
Start the typed-\fBDESTROY\fR fence to engage or disengage. Then type
.B DESTROY
exactly, then
.BR y .
Any other key at either step cancels and sends nothing. The wipe is a stub in
v1.
.SH MAIN MENU
Devices, Whitelist, Dry-run, Settings, Event log, Config, LUKS destroy (greyed
until configured), Arm (greyed while the config is invalid), Disarm, Reload,
Help, Quit. Arm, Disarm and Reload each ask for confirmation first.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, the interface is rendered without colour; armed/disarmed and hazard
states are always distinguished by glyph and word as well as colour.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR killbilld (8),
.BR killbillctl (1),
.BR killbill.conf (5)
.SH BUGS
